{"name":"Auberge","hex":"#3f3130","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"auberge","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An inn or hostel."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/auberge"}],"entries":[{"title":"Auberge Ravoux","blocks":[{"text":"The Auberge Ravoux is a French historic landmark located in the heart of the village of Auvers-sur-Oise. It is known as the House of Van Gogh because the Dutch painter Vincent van Gogh spent the last 70 days of his life as a lodger at the auberge. During his stay at Auvers, Van Gogh created more than 80 paintings and 64 sketches before shooting himself in the chest on 27 July 1890 and dying two days later on 29 July 1890. The auberge (inn) has been restored as a museum and tourist attraction. The room where Van Gogh lived and died has been restored and can be viewed by the public."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Auberge_ravoux.jpg/330px-Auberge_ravoux.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auberge_Ravoux"},{"title":"Auberge (restaurant)","blocks":[{"text":"Auberge was a restaurant in Amsterdam, Netherlands. It was a fine dining restaurant that was awarded one Michelin star in 1980 and 1981."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auberge_(restaurant)"},{"title":"Auberge (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Auberge is the eleventh studio album by British singer-songwriter Chris Rea, released in February 1991. The album, as well as the title song, is notable for its association with the Caterham Super Seven that Rea owned, which he called the \"Blue Seven\". The car appears on the album cover, illustrated in oil by motoring artist Alan Fearnley. The album makes several references to the car over several tracks, as well on the video of the title song, and its cover illustration was used for its adverts. In 2005, Rea sold the car in an auction."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/85/Auberge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auberge_(album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Portrait_of_Adeline_Ravoux%2C_by_Vincent_van_Gogh.jpg/500px-Portrait_of_Adeline_Ravoux%2C_by_Vincent_van_Gogh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Portrait_of_Adeline_Ravoux%2C_by_Vincent_van_Gogh.jpg/1280px-Portrait_of_Adeline_Ravoux%2C_by_Vincent_van_Gogh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Portrait_of_Adeline_Ravoux%2C_by_Vincent_van_Gogh.jpg/500px-Portrait_of_Adeline_Ravoux%2C_by_Vincent_van_Gogh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Vincent van Gogh: Portrait of Adeline Ravoux (Auvers, June 1890)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APortrait_of_Adeline_Ravoux%2C_by_Vincent_van_Gogh.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Auberge_Ravoux_in_Auvers-sur-Oise.jpg/500px-Auberge_Ravoux_in_Auvers-sur-Oise.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Auberge_Ravoux_in_Auvers-sur-Oise.jpg/500px-Auberge_Ravoux_in_Auvers-sur-Oise.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Auberge Ravoux c. 1890. From left to right: Arthur Gustave Ravoux, Germaine Ravoux, presumably Raoul Levert, Adeline Ravoux.[4] Vincent Levert may be one of the three men sitting on the right (© Institut Van Gogh).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAuberge_Ravoux_in_Auvers-sur-Oise.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Van_Gogh%27s_Room.jpg/500px-Van_Gogh%27s_Room.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Van_Gogh%27s_Room.jpg/1280px-Van_Gogh%27s_Room.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Van_Gogh%27s_Room.jpg/500px-Van_Gogh%27s_Room.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Vincent's room at the Auberge Ravoux","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVan_Gogh's_Room.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Le_R%C3%A9gional_7_August_1890.jpg/500px-Le_R%C3%A9gional_7_August_1890.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Le_R%C3%A9gional_7_August_1890.jpg/500px-Le_R%C3%A9gional_7_August_1890.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Le Régional report of Van Gogh's suicide and funeral 7 August 1890","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALe_R%C3%A9gional_7_August_1890.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Auberge_Ravoux_at_the_Place_de_la_Mairie_near_Rue_du_G%C3%A9n%C3%A9ral_de_Gaulle%2C_Auvers-sur-Oise_PK-F-B.00552.jpg/500px-Auberge_Ravoux_at_the_Place_de_la_Mairie_near_Rue_du_G%C3%A9n%C3%A9ral_de_Gaulle%2C_Auvers-sur-Oise_PK-F-B.00552.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Auberge_Ravoux_at_the_Place_de_la_Mairie_near_Rue_du_G%C3%A9n%C3%A9ral_de_Gaulle%2C_Auvers-sur-Oise_PK-F-B.00552.jpg/1280px-Auberge_Ravoux_at_the_Place_de_la_Mairie_near_Rue_du_G%C3%A9n%C3%A9ral_de_Gaulle%2C_Auvers-sur-Oise_PK-F-B.00552.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Auberge_Ravoux_at_the_Place_de_la_Mairie_near_Rue_du_G%C3%A9n%C3%A9ral_de_Gaulle%2C_Auve